        "eyebrow": "Nutrient guide",
        "title": "Vitamins",
        "lead": "<p>Vitamins are essential organic compounds that your body requires in small amounts to function properly. Because your body cannot produce most vitamins on its own, you must obtain them regularly through food or supplementation.</p><p>There are 13 essential vitamins divided into two main categories: water-soluble and fat-soluble. Each plays a distinct role in keeping your energy steady, supporting your immune system, and protecting your cells.</p><p>Maintaining adequate vitamin intake supports overall vitality and long-term wellness, helping your body perform at its best every day.</p>",
        "hero_image": "shopify://shop_images/Velobiotics-Hero-vitamins.png",
        "groups_title": "How they are grouped",
        "nutrients_title": "Meet each one",
        "benefits_title": "What they do for you",
        "benefits": "<ul><li><strong>Energy metabolism:</strong> B-group vitamins assist in converting food into daily physical energy and stamina.</li><li><strong>Immune system strength:</strong> Vitamin C and Vitamin D support natural immune defences against everyday environmental challenges.</li><li><strong>Bone and muscle health:</strong> Vitamin D and Vitamin K work together to maintain strong bones and healthy muscle function.</li><li><strong>Antioxidant protection:</strong> Vitamin C and Vitamin E protect cell membranes from oxidative stress.</li><li><strong>Skin and tissue vitality:</strong> Vitamin A and Biotin nourish skin, hair, and mucous membranes.</li></ul>",
        "sources_title": "Natural sources",
        "sources": "<p>A balanced diet rich in whole foods is the primary source of essential vitamins. Citrus fruits, leafy green vegetables, berries, legumes, and whole grains provide abundant Vitamin C and B-complex vitamins. Oily fish, eggs, dairy, nuts, seeds, and avocado supply valuable fat-soluble vitamins A, D, E, and K.</p><p>Including a diverse range of local staples—such as maize, sweet potatoes, spinach, pilchards, and fresh fruits—alongside international diet staples ensures a broad intake of vital micro-nutrients.</p>",
        "why_title": "Why supplement?",
        "why": "<p>Modern lifestyle factors can make it difficult to get all the vitamins your body needs from food alone. Intensive farming methods, extended food storage, and high-heat cooking can reduce the nutrient content of everyday meals.</p><p>Specific life stages and circumstances—such as pregnancy, ageing, restrictive diets, busy schedules, or reduced sun exposure—increase daily nutrient demands. Daily supplementation provides a reliable safety net to bridge these dietary gaps. Always check with your healthcare professional to tailor supplementation to your personal health needs.</p>",
        "syn_title": "Why probiotics make them work better",
        "syn_text": "Velobiotics pairs essential vitamins with live probiotic bacteria protected by patented micro-encapsulation technology. Healthy gut flora create an optimal intestinal environment for absorbing vitamins and minerals. Furthermore, beneficial gut bacteria naturally synthesize several B-complex vitamins and Vitamin K2 directly in your digestive tract. Micro-encapsulation shields each individual bacterium with a protective layer, ensuring live probiotics reach your gut intact to support optimal nutrient absorption.",
